      <p>If you're comparing format options for archiving, our <a href="/blog/epub-vs-pdf/">EPUB vs. PDF breakdown</a> covers when accessibility metadata matters most (spoiler: library distribution and educational contexts), and the <a href="/blog/calibre-vs-sigil-2026/">calibre vs. Sigil comparison</a> helps decide which tool fits your editing workflow. For batch conversion pipelines that need to stay current, the <a href="/blog/calibre-cli-batch-conversion/">calibre CLI guide</a> covers the flags that interact with the new EPUB output behavior.</p>

      <h2>How to Update Calibre</h2>
      <p>Calibre's built-in updater handles Windows and macOS. On Linux, the recommended path is Kovid Goyal's official binary installer, which stays current regardless of distribution package freezes:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Close any running calibre instances.</li>
        <li>Download the installer from <a href="https://calibre-ebook.com/download_linux">calibre-ebook.com/download_linux</a>.</li>
        <li>Run the installer as root — it removes the previous version and installs 9.18 system-wide.</li>
        <li>Launch calibre and verify the version in Preferences → Miscellaneous.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>For the full release notes including every ticket reference, see the official changelog at <a href="https://calibre-ebook.com/whats-new">calibre-ebook.com/whats-new</a>.</p>

